{"source":"github","project_id":"bigdataclass","target":"rstudio/bigdataclass","id":"pr/24","ref":24,"title":"🏗 Renaming file for use with GitHub pages","description":"Hi @edgararuiz ! Thanks for a great course: starting to use this as a basis of training for some colleagues at work so will hopefully be able to feedback some other suggestions!\r\n\r\nThis pull request looks pretty major, but it is actually fairly simple: by changing the name of the documentation from `book` to `docs`, you can use GitHub pages to view the documentation directly within the browser. I have done this for my fork here:\r\n\r\nhttps://dr-harper.github.io/bigdataclass/index.html\r\n\r\nIf you accept this request, you will just have to setup GitHub pages in the settings tab:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20046224/52855423-439fcb80-3119-11e9-83a6-8a9699fa2d88.png)\r\n\r\n","published_at":"2019-02-15T12:01:02Z","updated_at":"2019-06-16T13:22:55Z","url":"https://github.com/rstudio/bigdataclass/pull/24","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"dr-harper","merged_at":"2019-06-16T13:22:55Z","state":"MERGED"}}
